{
  "title": "Make generated API clients reproducible",
  "description": "A clean `make ui-unit-test` regenerated the API clients and \
changed five committed TypeScript declaration files only by switching string \
literal quotes. `scripts/generate-clients.sh` compiles the generated \
TypeScript with `npx --yes -p typescript tsc`, which can select a different \
compiler than the version recorded in ramekin-ui/package-lock.json. The \
repository also contains multiple OpenAPI generator configuration files with \
different generator versions, making the effective version harder to reason \
about. Generated output should not depend on whichever tool release npx \
resolves that day.\n\
\n\
Scope:\n\
- Compile with the lockfile-installed TypeScript toolchain through the \
existing uv/npx workflow, and ensure the OpenAPI generator version has one \
authoritative pin.\n\
- Keep generation atomic and preserve the existing generated-client layout. Do \
not hand-edit generated output.\n\
- Add a Makefile-backed clean-tree regeneration check suitable for CI or lint \
so drift fails visibly.\n\
- Regenerate once with the chosen pinned toolchain and commit any intentional \
generated diff.\n\
- Correct stale generation instructions or comments encountered in this path.\n\
\n\
This is tooling-only and should not alter the API schema or client behavior.",
